# Bounce route — sources and equations, 2026-09-07

Source extraction only: no feasibility decision, ranking, parameter survey, physics conclusion, or framework. Only the four named local records were read for the lane constraint; their referenced files were not opened. No census kit, repair, Hwao material, or unopened evaluation data was accessed.

## (A) Citations, publication status, and access evidence

**S1 — target and published anchor.** Nikodem J. Popławski, “A nonsingular, anisotropic universe in a black hole with torsion and particle production,” *General Relativity and Gravitation* **53**(2), article **18** (2021), DOI [10.1007/s10714-021-02790-7](https://doi.org/10.1007/s10714-021-02790-7). **Journal publication ESTABLISHED.** Publisher: received 14 December 2020, accepted 19 January 2021, published/version of record 7 February 2021. [arXiv:2007.11556v2](https://arxiv.org/html/2007.11556v2), revised 23 June 2026, identifies itself as the published version. Publisher full text was independently read: the extracted numbered bounce/shear/production expressions and geometry caveats are present there. This verifies the extracted material, not byte identity of the entire 2026 upload with the 2021 article. Access: R01, R02, R05.

**S2 — second target.** Nikodem Popławski, “Gravitational Collapse with Torsion and Universe in a Black Hole,” in Cosimo Bambi (ed.), *Regular Black Holes: Towards a New Paradigm of Gravitational Collapse*, Springer Series in Astrophysics and Cosmology, chapter 13, pp. **485–499** (Springer, Singapore, **2023**), DOI [10.1007/978-981-99-1596-5_13](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-981-99-1596-5_13). **Book-chapter publication ESTABLISHED; journal publication of this exact arXiv version NOT ESTABLISHED; chapter peer-review process NOT ESTABLISHED by the checked records.** Publisher first-online date: 7 July 2023. [arXiv:2307.12190v1](https://arxiv.org/html/2307.12190v1), submitted 23 July 2023, identifies that chapter. Publisher access exposed a preview, not numbered full text. S2 equations below are therefore **context manuscript transcriptions**, not independently verified journal equations. Access: R03, R04, R06, R11.

**S2J — related same-title journal record.** Nikodem Popławski, “Gravitational collapse with torsion and universe in a black hole,” *International Journal of Modern Physics A* **40**(32), **2544007** (**2025**), DOI [10.1142/S0217751X25440075](https://doi.org/10.1142/S0217751X25440075). **This journal article's publication ESTABLISHED by publisher-deposited Crossref metadata**, dated 17 September 2025. Author, title and abstract closely match S2; Crossref supplies no version relation. Publisher access returned HTTP 403. **Full-text identity and equation-number agreement with arXiv:2307.12190v1 NOT ESTABLISHED.** This metadata does not silently promote S2 to a checked journal version. Access: R06, R12, R13.

**S3 — published spinor anchor.** Nikodem Popławski, “Nonsingular, big-bounce cosmology from spinor-torsion coupling,” *Physical Review D* **85**(10), **107502** (2012), DOI [10.1103/PhysRevD.85.107502](https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.85.107502). **Journal publication ESTABLISHED**, published 29 May 2012. APS version-of-record PDF read directly, five pages labeled 107502-1 through 107502-5. Access: R07, R09.

**S4 — published formalism anchor.** Friedrich W. Hehl, Paul von der Heyde, G. David Kerlick, and James M. Nester, “General relativity with spin and torsion: Foundations and prospects,” *Reviews of Modern Physics* **48**(3), **393–416** (1976), DOI [10.1103/RevModPhys.48.393](https://doi.org/10.1103/RevModPhys.48.393). **Journal publication ESTABLISHED**, July 1976. APS PDF read; pp. 409–410 additionally rendered and visually inspected in memory to resolve mathematical OCR. Access: R08, R10.

**S5 — bibliographic production lead, not an equation-verified anchor here.** Nikodem Popławski, “Universe in a black hole in Einstein–Cartan gravity,” *The Astrophysical Journal* **832**(2), **96** (2016), DOI [10.3847/0004-637X/832/2/96](https://doi.org/10.3847/0004-637X/832/2/96). **Publication ESTABLISHED** by Crossref, dated 21 November 2016. IOP PDF access returned bot-challenge HTML despite HTTP 200; ADS returned 403. Only metadata/abstract and the arXiv abstract record were checked. The latter identifies 1410.3881v2 (26 May 2026) as published version. No equations are attributed to an unread publisher PDF. Access: R14, R15, R17, R18.

