### S2 — chapter manuscript context; publisher equation numbering unverified

Eq. (34) explicitly chooses r(τ,R)=a(τ)sin R; (30) is the closed isotropic FLRW interval. Eq. (38) is its Friedmann equation; (40) is its two-turning-point existence condition. Section VI defines a turning point by ȧ=0 and a bounce by ä>0 there (unnumbered). This is not S3's cusp prescription.

