## (E) What the checked sources do not supply

“Not found” is limited to full texts actually checked: S1 publisher/arXiv, S2 manuscript, S3 APS PDF, S4 APS PDF. It does not cover unread references or the whole literature.

- **No checked full text solves Bianchi I with shear and particle production together.** S1 develops KS with both effects and explicitly limits its geometry. S2 solves a closed-isotropic ansatz and discusses shear/production, without Bianchi I directional evolution. S3 is isotropic. S4 includes a spatially flat anisotropic shear/spin example and discusses production separately, without a coupled Bianchi I production solution. This does not erase S1's explicit anisotropic treatment.
- **No checked full text supplies a controlled, self-consistent interacting thermal spin closure at the bounce beyond the free-gas approximation.** S1/S2 use a spin-fluid prescription; S3 identifies a Dirac-spin square with n²; S4 discusses formal Dirac/semiclassical sources and averaging limitations. These are not the missing closure calculation.
- No full-text identity/equation-number match was established between S2 and S2J.
- No publisher equations were obtained for S5/S6; metadata cannot establish absence of an item from their unread full texts.
- S1 supplies no exact Bianchi IX replacement for its KS scenario; it proposes one.
- S2 prints no coefficient for its prose-only a⁻⁴ shear addition.
- S1/S2 do not derive their particular phenomenological βH⁴ law microscopically.
- The extracted target treatments do not supply a numerical varied-condition survey or general rotating, inhomogeneous collapse solution.
- This file supplies no replacement closure, feasibility judgment or new physics conclusion.

